# Generator env for regen-locks.sh: resolver + the build backend needed
# to read producers/pyproject.toml metadata without isolation.
pip-tools
hatchling

# Hold pip below 26.2 until pip-tools supports it.
#
# pip-tools drives pip's internal API. pip 26.2 (2026-07-29) added a
# required `allow_editables` keyword argument to
# RequirementCommand.make_requirement_preparer(), which pip-compile does
# not pass:
#
#   TypeError: RequirementCommand.make_requirement_preparer() missing 1
#   required keyword-only argument: 'allow_editables'
#
# `pip` is resolved into pip-tools.lock via --allow-unsafe, so without a
# bound the convergence loop upgrades it to the latest release; phase 2
# then installs that candidate and pip-compile crashes, which is why the
# hash-lock drift check has failed since pip 26.2 shipped.
#
# Upgrading the generator does not help: pip-tools' newest release
# (7.6.0, 2026-07-18) predates pip 26.2 and is equally affected. Both
# 7.5.3 and 7.6.0 declare only `pip>=22.2`, so the metadata provides no
# protection and the bound has to live here.
#
# Remove this pin once a pip-tools release advertises pip 26.2 support.
pip<26.2
